      "location": "Refutation 2.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "It says that “the only initial segment abc among cyclic conjugates starts at the first letter of r itself.” But the cyclic conjugate beginning at the fourth letter is abcxabc. Thus abc is an initial segment of both abcabcx=abc·abcx and abcxabc=abc·xabc; these give distinct ordered pairs in def-piece-in-a-symmetrised-presentation. The displayed abc is a piece, so this is not the claimed counterexample.",
