      "evidence": "The Given hypothesis supplies only a null word w and a minimal-area diagram D. The cited Greendlinger result requires a reduced diagram with freely reduced, nontrivial boundary, but the proof establishes neither condition before asserting “[L1] gives a face.” After deletion, step 2.1 repeats the assertion without showing the new diagram is reduced or has freely reduced boundary. This unsupported iteration is the core of the area bound.",
