      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "No nontriviality condition on the torsion element, nor nonempty-relator condition, is stated. For the empty relator set, the presentation ⟨x | ∅⟩ is vacuously symmetrised C'(1/6); its identity has finite order, but there is no defining relator whose root can occur in the claimed conclusion. The proof likewise only assumes “some n≥1 satisfies u^n=1,” which includes the identity.",
