      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The asserted second equivalence omits compactness. Z with its profinite topology has the neighbourhood basis nZ of open normal subgroups and each quotient Z/nZ is finite, yet it is not profinite: its canonical image is a proper dense nonclosed subspace of its compact completion. Thus the open-normal finite-quotient basis condition alone does not characterize profinite groups.",
