      "evidence": "The proof obtains a finite quotient of ker(ρ), then claims that “Pulling back the corresponding kernel gives a finite-index subgroup K′≤K containing H but not g.” A quotient of ker(ρ) provides no homomorphism from K to that quotient, and its kernel need not be invariant under conjugation by H; hence there is no stated pullback subgroup of K containing H. The cited residual finiteness does not supply this required separation construction.",
